  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Lingering showers across the southern tier \ngradually taper off tonight into tomorrow, giving way to dry \nweather to end the week. Coastal storm effects still look like \nthey will stay mainly east of PA.\n\nHigh pressure and drier air moving down from the north will \nstart to dominate the forecast for the next 7 days. Lingering \nSHRA over the southern tier tonight will pose no heavy rain \nthreat. Any -RA left over in the morning could be entirely \nsouth of the CWA. We'll start to see high clouds from the \ncoastal low on Friday or even before then. We are leaving in the\nNBM 20 PoPs for the east for the weekend for places E of the \nSusq R without any confidence to totally drop mentions of it.",
